## Mutation Analysis

The mutation removes a `__syncthreads()` call at line 77 in the original code. Looking at the original reduce_loss_kernel:

```cpp
template<typename T>
__global__ void reduce_loss_kernel(
    const T* __restrict__ per_sample_loss,
    T* __restrict__ final_loss,
    int batch_size
) {
    __shared__ T shared[256];

    int tid = threadIdx.x;
    int idx = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + tid;

    T val = 0;
    if (idx < batch_size) {
        val = per_sample_loss[idx];
    }

    shared[tid] = val;
    __syncthreads();  // LINE ~72 - This is KEPT

    // Block reduction
    for (int stride = blockDim.x / 2; stride > 0; stride >>= 1) {
        if (tid < stride) {
            shared[tid] += shared[tid + stride];
        }
        __syncthreads();  // LINE 77 - This is REMOVED in the mutant!
    }

    if (tid == 0) {
        atomicAdd(final_loss, shared[0] / batch_size);
    }
}
```

The mutated code removes the `__syncthreads()` inside the reduction loop. This is a critical synchronization - without it, threads may read stale values from shared memory during the reduction.

